No live site exists. Every item is a pre-launch recommendation, not an observed defect. No crawl or Core Web Vitals data was collected.

| # | Check | Severity | Pre-launch recommendation |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Indexation and canonical | Critical | Staging must send `noindex` (meta robots or `X-Robots-Tag`); production needs a self-referential `<link rel="canonical">` and a robots.txt that declares the sitemap. Owner: Deniz. |
| 2 | Meta title | High | `Pet Sitters Near You: ID-Checked and Reviewed | PetPal` (53 chars). Primary term first, brand suffix. "ID-checked" awaits Defne's review. |
| 3 | Meta description | High | `Find a pet sitter to care for your pet at home. Every sitter is ID-checked, and you can read owner reviews first. Free to search.` (129 chars) |
| 4 | Heading hierarchy | Medium | One `<h1>`: the hero headline "Trusted sitters, happy pets, calm owners." It has no search term, so put "pet sitter" in the subhead or the first H2. Owner: Kaan with Deniz. |
| 5 | Structured data and internal link | Low | Add the FAQPage block below only if the same Q&As are visible on the page. Link to the pillar `/guides/choose-a-pet-sitter` (Yavuz's unconfirmed assumption: confirm the slug before linking). |

## FAQPage JSON-LD

```json
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is a pet sitter or a kennel better for my pet?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on your pet and how it handles unfamiliar places. A sitter keeps your pet at home, while a kennel can suit some pets. Our guide compares both."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What should I ask a pet sitter before the first booking?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Ask about experience, emergencies, routines and medication, and how they will keep in touch. Watch for vague answers."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do ID checks and reviews work on PetPal?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "PLACEHOLDER: replace with the verification steps once Defne confirms what PetPal actually does."
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
Q3 holds a placeholder: do not publish until Defne confirms the steps. Validated by parsing the block with `node` (`JSON.parse`).

